      "before": "Author-side disposition: CONDITIONAL_VIEW_LOCAL_ACTION_CLASSIFIED; NATIVE_EVENT_AND_ACCESS_NOT_DERIVED.",
      "after": "Reviewed disposition: CONDITIONAL_VIEW_LOCAL_ACTION_CLASSIFIED; NATIVE_EVENT_AND_ACCESS_NOT_DERIVED."
    },
    {
      "line": 114,
      "before": "The next physical obligation is specific: justify access to the common-carrier/global-leaf information and an event mechanism whose action is H_T (or a separately justified member/relation), together with retained use of its output. A proof of universal safety alone is insufficient, and adding maximal deletion as an axiom is not authorized. The old consumer additionally needs justified cross-view redundancy information if its global-leaf deletion is retained as the goal. Which information is physically available must be derived before treating either architecture as native.",
      "after": "The next physical obligation is specific: justify access to the common-carrier/global-leaf information and an event mechanism whose action is H_T (or a separately justified member/relation), together with retained use of its output. A proof of universal safety alone is insufficient, and adding maximal deletion as an axiom is not authorized. The old consumer requires leaving the universal view-local class, for example through justified cross-view redundancy information or a justified restricted input promise; the theorem does not mandate one particular replacement architecture. Which information is physically available must be derived before treating either architecture as native."
    },
    {
      "line": 118,
      "before": "Exact inspected sources are in source_readbacks.json. The use of the old pruning-cone and endpoint theorems is explicit, and their historical execution status is not recertified here.",
      "after": "Exact inspected sources are in view_local_pruning/source_readbacks.json. The use of the old pruning-cone and endpoint theorems is explicit, and their historical execution status is not recertified here."
    }
